xercising the happy‑path where no branch adds a message.'}, {'input': [{'parameter': 'rootNode', 'value': '{ "age": "twenty" }'}], 'expected': "Set containing two ValidationMessages: (1) required property 'name' is missing, (2) type mismatch for 'age' (expected integer, found string)", 'description': 'Both the required‑validator and type‑validator branches are triggered because the required property is absent and the present property has the wrong type.'}]}, {'group': 'Schema with $ref (reference) resolution', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'rootNode', 'value': '{ "address": { "city": "NY" } }'}], 'expected': 'Empty Set – the referenced schema for "address" resolves correctly and validates successfully', 'description': 'The schema contains a $ref to an external definition for "address". The JSON instance matches that definition, causing the reference‑resolution branch to succeed.'}, {'input': [{'parameter': 'rootNode', 'value': '{ "address": { "zip": 12345 } }'}], 'expected': 'Set containing a ValidationMessage with message "required property \'city\' is missing in referenced schema \'address\'"', 'description': "The $ref branch is exercised, but the instance fails the referenced schema's required property, producing an error."}]}, {'group': 'Dynamic anchor handling', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'rootNode', 'value': '{ "type": "cat" }'}], 'expected': 'Empty Set – dynamic anchor resolves to the correct subschema and validates', 'description': 'Schema uses a dynamic anchor (e.g., "$dynamicAnchor": "pet") that points to a subschema requiring "type" to be one of ["cat","dog"]. The instance matches, testing the dynamic‑anchor branch.'}, {'input': [{'parameter': 'rootNode', 'value': '{ "type": "rock" }'}], 'expected': 'Set containing a ValidationMessage with message "enum mismatch: value \'rock\' is not allowed"', 'description': 'The same dynamic anchor is used, but the instance violates the enum constraint, exercising the failure path of the dynamic‑anchor branch.'}]}, {'group': 'Discriminator validation (polymorphic schemas)', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'rootNode', 'value': '{ "petType": "dog", "bark": true }'}], 'expected': 'Empty Set – discriminator selects the correct subschema and validation passes', 'description': 'Schema defines a discriminator on property "petType" with mapping to subschemas for "dog" and "cat". The instance selects "dog" and satisfies its subschema, testing the discriminator branch.'}, {'input': [{'parameter': 'rootNode', 'value': '{ "petType": "cat", "bark": true }'}], 'expected': 'Set containing a ValidationMessage with message "property \'meow\' is required for discriminator value \'cat\'"', 'description': 'Discriminator selects the "cat" subschema, but the instance provides a property belonging to the "dog" subschema, causing the discriminator‑validation branch to emit an error.'}]}, {'group': 'Schema with additionalProperties = false', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'rootNode', 'value': '{ "known": 1 }'}], 'expected': 'Empty Set – only defined properties are present', 'description': 'Schema disallows additional properties. The instance contains only the defined property, exercising the branch that skips additional‑property checks.'}, {'input': [{'parameter': 'rootNode', 'value': '{ "known": 1, "extra": "value" }'}], 'expected': 'Set containing a ValidationMessage with message "additional property \'extra\' is not allowed"', 'description': 'The same schema encounters an unexpected property, triggering the additional‑properties‑false branch.'}]}, {'group': 'Pattern validation', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'rootNode', 'value': '{ "code": "AB1234" }'}], 'expected': 'Empty Set – the string matches the regex pattern ^[A-Z]{2}\\d{4}$', 'description': 'Schema defines property "code" with a pattern that requires two uppercase letters followed by four digits. The instance value conforms, exercising the successful pattern‑validator path.'}, {'input': [{'parameter': 'rootNode', 'value': '{ "code": "ab12" }'}], 'expected': 'Set containing a ValidationMessage with message "pattern mismatch: value \'ab12\' does not match \'^\\\\[A-Z]{2}\\\\d{4}$\'"', 'description': 'The same pattern constraint is applied, but the instance value does not satisfy the regex, triggering the pattern‑validator branch.'}]}, {'group': 'Array items and size validation', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'rootNode', 'value': '[ 1, 2, 3 ]'}], 'expected': 'Empty Set – all items are integers and array length respects minItems=1 and maxItems=5', 'description': 'Schema defines an array of integers with minItems=1, maxItems=5, and each item must be of type integer. The instance meets both size and item‑type constraints.'}, {'input': [{'parameter': 'rootNode', 'value': '[ 1, "two", 3, 4, 5, 6 ]'}], 'expected': 'Set containing two ValidationMessages: (1) type mismatch for item at index 1 (expected integer, found string), (2) array size exceeds maxItems of 5', 'description': 'The array contains a string among integers (type‑validator failure) and has six elements, violating the maxItems constraint, exercising multiple validator branches.'}]}, {'group': 'Enum and const validation', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'rootNode', 'value': '"RED"'}], 'expected': 'Empty Set – value is one of the allowed enum values ["RED","GREEN","BLUE"]', 'description': 'Schema defines an enum of colour strings. The instance value "RED" is permitted, testing the enum‑validator happy path.'}, {'input': [{'parameter': 'rootNode', 'value': '"YELLOW"'}], 'expected': 'Set containing a ValidationMessage with message "enum mismatch: value \'YELLOW\' is not among the allowed values"', 'description': 'The same enum constraint is applied, but the instance value is not listed, causing an enum‑validation error.'}, {'input': [{'parameter': 'rootNode', 'value': '42'}], 'expected': 'Set containing a ValidationMessage with message "const mismatch: value 42 does not equal the required constant 100"', 'description': 'Schema defines a const value of 100. The instance provides 42, exercising the const‑validator failure branch.'}]}, {'group': 'Composite keywords (allOf / anyOf / oneOf)', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'rootNode', 'value': '{ "age": 30, "email": "user@example.com" }'}], 'expected': 'Empty Set – instance satisfies all subschemas combined via allOf', 'description': 'Schema uses allOf to require both a numeric "age" (minimum 0) and a string "email" matching an email format. The instance meets both, testing the allOf aggregation.'}, {'input': [{'parameter': 'rootNode', 'value': '"short"'}], 'expected': 'Empty Set – instance satisfies at least one subschema in anyOf (e.g., string with minLength 5 or integer > 10) because it matches the integer subschema after coercion is not applied, but matches the string subschema with minLength 5? Actually "short" length 5 satisfies minLength 5, so passes.', 'description': 'Schema defines anyOf with two alternatives: a string with minLength 5, or an integer greater than 10. The instance is a string of length 5, satisfying one alternative, exercising the anyOf success path.'}, {'input': [{'parameter': 'rootNode', 'value': '15'}], 'expected': 'Set containing a ValidationMessage with message "oneOf validation failed: instance matches 2 subschemas, expected exactly 1"', 'description': 'Schema defines oneOf with two mutually exclusive subschemas (integer > 10 and integer < 20). The value 15 satisfies both, violating the oneOf rule and triggering the corresponding validation error.'}]}, {'group': 'Conditional validation (if/then/else)', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'rootNode', 'value': '{ "type": "premium", "discount": 20 }'}], 'expected': 'Empty Set – condition matches (type == "premium") and then‑schema validates discount property', 'description': 'Schema uses if to check "type" equals "premium"; then requires a numeric "discount" between 0 and 50. The instance satisfies both the condition and the then‑branch.'}, {'input': [{'para